---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'What is the best way to clean stainless steel cutlery?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Hand washing with warm water and mild soap is the gentlest option. Silver-tone pieces can tolerate more regular daily use, but abrasive scrubbers and harsh chemicals should always be avoided.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Can wenge wood handle cutlery go in the dishwasher?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'No. Wenge wood handle pieces should be hand washed only. Long exposure to hot water and dishwasher cycles can dry, warp, or damage the wooden handle over time.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Is the gold tone made of real gold?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: "No. The 'silver' and 'gold' refer to the tone of the finish — silver tone and gold tone — not the actual metal. For carved 5-piece sets, the knife uses 410 stainless steel while the fork and spoon pieces use 304 stainless steel; see each product page for SKU details.",
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'What is 304 stainless steel?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: '304 stainless steel is a food-grade alloy containing 18% chromium and 8% nickel. It is highly resistant to rust, corrosion, and staining — making it the industry standard for quality cutlery and kitchenware.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'How should I care for gold-tone cutlery?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Gold-tone pieces should be hand washed with mild soap and dried immediately. Avoid soaking, bleach, and abrasive cleaners to help preserve the finish.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'How often should I oil wooden handles?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'If your wenge wood handles begin to look dry, a small amount of food-safe mineral oil can be applied occasionally. This is a maintenance step, not something needed after every wash.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Does stainless steel cutlery need to be dried right away?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Yes. Drying promptly helps maintain surface clarity and reduces water spotting, especially on polished finishes and decorative details.',
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Is Yinshiji cutlery suitable for daily use?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Absolutely. Yinshiji stainless steel pieces are designed for daily use. Product pages list the exact grade by SKU — including carved-set knives made with 410 stainless steel and fork/spoon pieces made with 304 stainless steel.',
    },
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs,
};

const alternateLinks = [
  { lang: 'en', href: '/materials-care' },
  { lang: 'zh-CN', href: '/zh/materials-care' },
  { lang: 'x-default', href: '/materials-care' },
];

const navItems = [
  { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
  { href: '/products', label: 'Products' },
  { href: '/guide', label: 'Guide' },
  { href: '/reference', label: 'Reference' },
  { href: '/about', label: 'About' },
  { href: '/materials-care', label: 'Materials & Care' },
  { href: '/faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Materials & Care – Yinshiji | Stainless Steel & Wenge Wood Cutlery Guide"
  description="Learn about the materials and proper care for Yinshiji cutlery. Guide to stainless steel grades, silver tone and gold tone finishes, wenge wood handles, and maintenance best practices."
  ogType="website"
  lang="en"
  homeUrl="/"
  navItems={navItems}
  alternateLinks={alternateLinks}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:3rem;">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="section-title">Materials &amp; Care</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Good tableware should not only look right on the table — it should also hold up in real life.
          This guide explains how we think about stainless steel grades, gold-tone finishes, and wenge wood
          handles, plus the simple care habits that help each piece last longer.
        </p>

        <h2>Stainless Steel Grades</h2>
        <p>
          Yinshiji uses stainless steel according to the product structure. Fork and spoon pieces in the carved
          collections use <strong>304 stainless steel</strong>, while the carved-set dinner knife uses
          <strong>410 stainless steel</strong>. Each product page lists the exact material for that SKU.
          304 is widely used for food-contact cutlery because it resists corrosion well and holds up to daily use. 410 is
          used for the carved-set knives because knife hardness and blade structure are different from
          forks and spoons.
        </p>

        <h2>Silver Tone &amp; Gold Tone</h2>
        <p>
          The silver and gold collections are both stainless steel at their core. The difference is the
          surface presentation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Silver tone</strong> is the most straightforward option for daily use: cleaner,
          quieter, easier to maintain, and visually closer to the natural look of polished steel.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Gold tone</strong> is a warm surface finish over stainless steel. It is used for color
          and atmosphere, not to imitate precious metal. For that reason, it should be treated more
          gently than silver tone pieces.
        </p>

        <h2>Wenge Wood Handles</h2>
        <p>
          Our wenge wood handle pieces combine stainless steel working ends with a natural wood grip.
          The idea is to make the fork feel warmer in hand — less cold metal, more natural grip.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because wood is a natural material, grain and tone will vary slightly from piece to piece.
          That variation is part of the character of the product, not a defect.
        </p>

        <h2>Daily Care Principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Wash with mild soap and warm water.</li>
          <li>Dry soon after washing to reduce spots and keep the finish clearer.</li>
          <li>Avoid bleach, harsh acids, and abrasive scrubbers.</li>
          <li>Gold-tone pieces should be hand washed for better finish longevity.</li>
          <li>Wenge wood handle pieces should never be soaked or put in a dishwasher.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why This Matters</h2>
        <p>
          Yinshiji is rooted in Jieyang, Guangdong, where stainless steel manufacturing is part of the local industry.
          Being close to that supply chain means we can be more specific about materials and care —
          things we prefer to say honestly rather than gloss over.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
